# Exact-Q closure of the nonconstant k=4-ray rows K=8 and K=9

Date: 2026-09-04  
Lane: `k4ray-K89-sol56-20260903`  
Status: complete; both rows decided by exact-Q unit certificates

## Verdict at a glance

This lane replaces the 58- and 74-variable top-pin computations by exact
lower-band parametrizations before asking for a standard basis.

| row | reduced necessary chart | characteristic-zero decision | consequence |
|---|---:|---|---|
| K=8, b=6, D=108 no-split `(24,16;18;7;4)` | 36 ring variables; 61 band rows plus the `mu` localizer | **`UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`** | row dead; D=108 closed at skeleton level |
| K=9, b=7, `(99,66)` case (A), internal split A | 36 variables; 96 rows plus localizer | **`UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`** | internal chart dead |
| K=9, b=7, `(99,66)` case (A), internal split B | 36 variables; 98 rows plus localizer | **`UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0`** | internal chart dead; case (A) dead |

None of these decisions is a modular lift. In every row three good finite-field
fibres die, and a separate standard-basis computation over `Q` gives the
one-element basis `[1]`, `dim=-1`, and `reduce(I,G)=0`. The modular computations
are recorded only as screens because the charts contain the inhomogeneous
equation `mu*mu_inv-1`.

## Scope and decision standard

This report records the reduced-chart construction, staged and modular screens,
mandatory exact-rational decisions, controls, and any resulting skeleton
promotions for the two outstanding nonconstant arms:

- K=8, D=108 no-split `(24,16; 18; 7; 4)`, b=6;
- K=9, case (A) of `(99,66)`, `(27,18; 21; 8; 4)`, b=7.

Only an exact-Q unit certificate closes a row as dead.  Positive-dimensional
output is followed by point extraction and an exact Jacobian test.  Finite-field
unit output is used only as a screen and is never promoted directly.

