box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/compute-notes.md:9:- Independent enumeration at `(75,50)` gives 682 `(1)--(7)` assignments and no occurrence of `delta_1=1/3`.  The printed row with `M_2=55,V_2=2,V_3=4` has `delta_1=2/3`.
box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/compute-notes.md:67:The generated survivor file has SHA-256 `22c80f9893966cb1ae17322dfd8f6ac806e74c907ce61724dfcac236bfa14124`.  It differs from the frozen survivor artifact only in the first three header lines (`V_2` and line wrapping); `tail -n +4` is byte-identical.
box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/compute-notes.md:92:At `(n,m)=(75,50)` it finds 682 `(1)--(7)` assignments.  The exact `M_2` support is
box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/compute-notes.md:125:6. printed `(99,66; M2=77; V2=8,V3=8)`;
box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/compute-notes.md:144:- **TOP-SPLIT:** `V_s<d_s`.  It is already automatic in the frozen enumeration: 658 -> 658.
box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/compute-notes.md:145:- **TOP-RADIUS:** `(d_s-V_s)(n-M_{s-1})>=d_s`.  Also automatic: 658 -> 658.
box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/compute-notes.md:152:Starting with the top `V_s`, at each `j=s-1,...,2` recompute the radius and `A_j` on the synthetic zero path, let `P=V_{j+1}d_j/d_{j+1}`, and let `b=P mod A_j` be the canonical nonnegative zero multiplicity.  If `b=0` or `b<=d_j/(n-M_j)`, the forced all-zero major path stops.  Otherwise set `V_j=b` and continue; reject if it remains major to the bottom.
box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/compute-notes.md:254:The pinned-N test additionally empties candidate-active degrees `72,80`.  Thus the complete all-empty list is the preceding list plus `72,80`.
