+# (99,66) N1 skeleton enumeration and partial computational closure
+
+Date: 2026-09-04
+
+Lane: `g9966-n1-skeletons-gpt55-20260903`
+
+Status: `PARTIAL`
+
+## Verdict
+
+The frozen Moh enumerator confirms the N1 premise: at `(n,m)=(99,66)`,
+Moh's printed conditions `(1)-(13)` admit exactly eight characteristic-data
+assignments. The banked row is the published/Moh-selected row
+
+```text
+M=(-66,77,97),  d=(99,33,11,1),  V_3=8, V_2=8,  u_s=3, v_s=8.
+```
+
+Among the seven non-`(8,8)` rows, this lane kills exactly one:
+
+```text
+S6: M=(-66,55,97), V_3=10, V_2=2, u_s=1
+    -> descended row (9,6; M_2'=5, V_2'=2; k=2)
+    -> full order-basis partition [1]
+    -> three finite-field unit screens plus exact-Q UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0.
+```
+
+The other six non-banked rows remain typed `OPEN`. Therefore N1 is **not**
+closed here, and no degree-wide `(99,66)` theorem is promoted. The degree-wide
+milestone would be notify-worthy only after all seven non-banked rows are dead;
+that did not happen in this lane.
+
