+## Triage
+
+S5 and S6 are `u_s=1` rows. They have no genuine split of the principal-minor
+packet. The applicable instrument is the Prop 6.3/6.4 descent to a
+monomial-Jacobian order chart, implemented here by the corrected full
+order-basis emitter from `order_basis_full.py` and replayed through
+`box/lib/guided_gb.py`.
+
+S1, S2, S3, S4, and S7 are `u_s>=2` rows. A full skeleton death would require
+two disjoint duties:
+
+```text
+split branch:
+  a joint two-point chart or minor-root classification at every detector order
+  listed in the enumeration table;
+
+unsplit branch:
+  the pin + lower-band + guided_gb method on the descended row listed above.
+```
+
+The banked joint chart and K=9 pin/lower-band certificates do not transfer by
+matching only `u_s` or the split-order set. Their chart hypotheses include the
+banked row's actual `M_2=77,V_3=8,V_2=8` data and the descended
+`(27,18;21;8;k=4)` row. S4 has the same `(u_s,v_s)=(3,8)` split-order window
+as S8, but it descends to `(27,18;6;1;k=19)`, so it is not the banked chart.
+
+The auxiliary integration `N` screen from `moh_skeleton_full.py` was also
+checked. It is useful as a priority signal only. Some non-banked groups have
+no mixed `N in [6,16]`, but this report does not promote those screens as
+deaths because no charged source in this lane supplies the necessary promotion
+hook for these rows.
